<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">11032026</say-as>.</s> <s>The twenty-second of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran's Revolutionary Guards have declared the Strait of Hormuz closed until the war ends — no longer a pressure tactic, but a formal wartime condition, with Iran's foreign minister confirming that negotiations are off the table.</s> <s>Simultaneously, Israel announced it has destroyed half of Iran's ballistic missile stockpile and has shifted its campaign to targeting regime infrastructure — government ministries and the political commands of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps — aiming at collapse or capitulation.</s> <s>Day sixteen has changed what ending this war might look like.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>One hundred thousand people fled Lebanon in a single day — the fastest single-day displacement of the entire conflict — bringing the total uprooted since early March to more than seven hundred thousand.</s> <s>Israel has been issuing evacuation orders with no safe corridors, giving families minutes to move before bombardment follows.</s> <s>The World Health Organization warns that a hundred and twenty thousand people crowded into government shelters now face acute disease outbreak risk.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia is drawing up contingency plans for its two hundred and twenty thousand pilgrims as the conflict in the Persian Gulf bears down on Hajj season, with the first departures scheduled for April twenty-second.</s> <s>The pilgrimage has been suspended only twice since nineteen seventy-nine — and never before because of active war in the region.</s> <s>Saudi Arabia has not yet said whether it can safely host two million worshippers while simultaneously defending its oil infrastructure.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Inside Iran, dozens have been arrested on espionage charges since the war began, as authorities move to silence internal dissent.</s> <s>The police chief warned that dissidents would be treated as enemy combatants after the United States publicly called on Iranians to overthrow their government.</s> <s>Foreign nationals have also been detained; no formal charges have been disclosed in any case.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria has begun evacuating its citizens from Iran, with embassy officials escorting them across the Armenian border as commercial air routes close.</s> <s>Pakistan, Singapore, and the Philippines are running parallel evacuations; for many of these workers, their remittances are the primary income keeping families afloat at home.</s> <s>The Nigerian government has not disclosed how many of its citizens remain inside the country.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chile's newly inaugurated president, José Antonio Kast, launched a ninety-day emergency plan built around security, fiscal austerity, and stricter migration controls — completing a sharp rightward turn five years after a social uprising swept the left to power.</s> <s>Brazil's President Lula boycotted the ceremony after learning that Flávio <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="boʊl.soˈnɑːroʊ">Bolsonaro</phoneme> — his likely rival in Brazil's twenty twenty-six election — was on the guest list.</s> <s>Argentina's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="miˈleɪ">Milei</phoneme> and Venezuelan opposition leader María Corina <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑˈtʃɑː.doʊ">Machado</phoneme> were there, cementing a visible right-wing axis across the continent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>North Korea launched a cruise missile from a naval destroyer — the first time Pyongyang has fired a strategic weapon from a surface vessel, a platform far harder to pre-empt than a fixed land-based launch site.</s> <s>The test extends North Korea's potential strike range and comes while the United States military remains consumed by the war in the Persian Gulf.</s> <s>Washington has not publicly responded.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Oil hit one hundred and nineteen dollars a barrel this week — up fifty percent since January — as the declared Hormuz blockade removed any near-term expectation of a diplomatic resolution.</s> <s>Central banks face a stagflation trap: cutting interest rates risks fuelling inflation, while raising them deepens any recession.</s> <s>Markets now price an eighty percent probability of European Central Bank rate hikes — double the figure before the war began.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Saudi Aramco activated its East-West bypass pipeline, capable of carrying four and a half million barrels daily to the Red Sea without passing through the strait.</s> <s>Iraq, Kuwait, and Bahrain have no comparable bypass and have halted exports entirely; Qatar declared force majeure on its share of global liquefied natural gas supply.</s> <s>The blockade is not distributing pain equally — Riyadh emerges with structural leverage over its Gulf neighbours that it did not hold a fortnight ago.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United Kingdom's coal use fell last year to its lowest level since sixteen hundred — four centuries of industrial records broken in a single year, with wind and solar driving total emissions to their lowest since eighteen seventy-two.</s> <s>But the Iran war has since doubled gas prices, threatening to reverse those gains at the very moment the energy transition was accelerating.</s> <s>Analysts note the United Kingdom met only nine of the fifteen million tonnes of annual emissions cuts required to stay on its net-zero pathway.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's new five-year climate plan targets a seventeen percent reduction in carbon intensity by twenty thirty — a metric that permits absolute emissions to keep rising by three to six percent.</s> <s>Energy emissions have already fallen for twenty-one consecutive months, a baseline scientists called encouraging.</s> <s>Independent experts described the immediate twenty twenty-six annual target as alarmingly lax and inconsistent with any one-and-a-half-degree warming pathway.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China reportedly sold Iran a supersonic anti-ship missile capable of Mach four, able to cover the entire Persian Gulf from Iran's coastline — giving United States warships drastically less warning than Iran's existing subsonic arsenal.</s> <s>Beijing denied the report but has not said whether any agreement was finalized.</s> <s>If the sale is confirmed, the threat calculus for every naval vessel operating in the Gulf has fundamentally changed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two artificial intelligence findings this week challenge how the industry measures progress.</s> <s>A startup demonstrated a full language model running on consumer Apple Silicon hardware at five hundred and fifty tokens per second — matching cloud inference speeds without a data centre.</s> <s>Separately, a researcher topped a major benchmark leaderboard simply by duplicating seven middle layers of an existing model with no additional training, gaining eight percent in mathematical reasoning and raising the question of whether these benchmarks measure genuine capability or something considerably easier to engineer.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>